9 (mduppre) |\n| **Region** | USGOVVirginia |\n| **Build** | B:2602.0.7 / O:Dell / C:Internal |\n\n---\n\n### Problem Description\n\nCustomer is **blocked from deleting an orphaned network interface** (\u0060arcvm001-NIC\u0060) after VM \u0060arcvm001\u0060 was deleted from the portal.\n\n**Root Cause:** After upgrading from Azure Local **2512 \u2192 2601**, a new infrastructure LNET (\u0060ceo-clu001-Infra-LNET\u0060) was auto-created with an **IP range that overlaps** the pre-existing \u0060LNET1-Static\u0060.\n\nWhen attempting to remove the NIC, the webhook validator rejects the operation:\n\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\ncreateupdatevalidationwebhook.infrastructure.azstackhci.microsoft.com denied the request:\nThe following IP Pool ranges you entered are already in use: [10.10.35.52, 10.10.35.61]\nby ceo-clu001-InfraLNET. Please choose different ranges to avoid conflicts.\n\u0060\u0060\u0060\n\n---\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\n- **Blast radius:** Low \u2014 this is an **internal Dell test stamp** in USGOVVirginia, not a production customer environment\n- **Customer impact:** Resource cleanup is blocked (cannot delete orphaned NIC)\n- **Logs access:** Restricted \u2014 stamp is in USGovVirginia, logs cannot be accessed directly\n\n---\n\n### Environment\n\n- **Cluster:** \u0060/subscriptions/f726effd-d97f-48c1-8f47-e0bb67d2fe33/resourceGroups/choliv-test-rg/providers/microsoft.azurestackhci/clusters/ceo-clu001\u0060\n- **Upgrade path:** Azure Local 2512 \u2192 2601\n\n---\n\n### Mitigation / Ask\n\n1. Help needed to **delete the orphaned NIC** (\u0060arcvm001-nic\u0060) via portal\n2. Investigate whether the **LNET IP range overlap** introduced during the 2601 upgrade is blocking the NIC deletion webhook validation\n3. Potential fix: Remove or resolve the conflicting IP pool ranges in \u0060ceo-clu001-InfraLNET\u0060 to allow the webhook to pass, enabling NIC deletion\n\n---\n\n**Files saved to:** \u0060E:\\icms\\Azure_Stack_HCI\\Arc_Managed_VMs\\783872773\\\u0060\n\n[OUTP